                <pb facs="0257" n="247" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg247"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">722.2315/2633: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-05T23:00:00-05:00">December 5, 1941—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 5—10:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>496. Department’s telegram 368, December 4, 2 p.m. Doctor Tobar accepts the
                    addition of Chile to the countries which are kindly extending their good offices
                    in the boundary matter.</p>
                <p>I am led to believe that the suggestion about including Mexico has been
                    withdrawn.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Lima.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
